                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "just got it on PC, I have it already on Switch bundled with Eschatos.\nJudgement Silversword has very smooth gameplay, and a lot of fun. You can see how it evolved into Eschatos. Similar enemies, patterns, no bomb just a shield to get through bullets, and broken up into short stages that come at you very fast. Basically its old school Eschatos with 2d graphics.\nCardinal Sins is one I have spent less time with, I think its mostly for competing with yourself or a friend. I think it is called a Caravan SHMUP? You get graded on each Stage. if you die it goes onto the next stage, and the next, and then you get your score for each stage at the end. It's okay but I prefer Judgement Silversword.\n\nI recommend these games, but only after you have gotten the other SHMUPs by Qute- Eschatos, Ginga Force, Natsuki Chronicles, and want more.",
